    "outline": {
      "widthMm": 100,
      "heightMm": 82,
      "thicknessMm": 1.6,
      "sizeReason": {
        "kind": "routing",
        "detail": "The 100x80 mm board (rev 21) was built and failed: the autorouter ran out of room around the motor driver U5. The trace from U5 VM to C4 pin2 was 8.50 mm and from U5 VCP to C4 pin1 6.01 mm, both over the 5 mm maximum, and a via overlapped J1 pin10. Earlier builds: the 90x72 mm board (rev 15) failed JLCPCB 2-layer DRC (hole clearance 0.1712 mm against 0.2 mm); the 80x66 mm board (rev 14) and the 70x60 mm board (rev 10) failed the same way. This 100x82 mm board grows the height by 2 mm to give the router room around U5 and the USB-C connector."
      }
    },
    "parts": [
      {
